note('Author page 5, archive 50. A cancelled orientation-identification paragraph precedes definitions of four families of simple paths, with cardinalities 12, 6, 6 and 6, the action of τ, and endpoint descriptions (23)–(27). The marginal Rep(J) map records the cyclic ordering i→j→k. The marginal number is read (22), even though the main τ display also bears (22); no numbering is regularised. The definition (27) is enclosed by a rounded frame. In the cutting notation the upper replacement is read Dec, whereas the later occurrence has a clearly dotted i, Dic; the top form has medium confidence. The cancellation under (24) remains doubtful in its old Σ_R symbol. The c,d families are indexed by ε in (21) but by ω in (25)–(26), as both written displays show. The final paragraph says that the endpoints of c_i^ω,d_i^ω lie on the boundary, although (25) gives c:P^ω—Q_i, with interior endpoints; the likely intended list is tilde b,d, but c remains in the transcription. H supplies an arrowhead in (25) absent from the ink. The first endpoint of (27) is unprimed omega, and the tilde on its path is present. No external result was used to settle a reading.')
hand('G, omega and abbreviated cutting notation','Scan 051 gives particularly clear G_J forms: the upper loop and internal bar belong to G, with no independent tilde. The opening surface-orientation set has both a bar above omega and an underline below; this differs from the underlined cyclic-order omega. A dot above the middle letter establishes Dic in the later cutting formula, while the upper insertion looks like Dec. These forms are preserved separately rather than silently regularised.')
